# drumming Peregian Originals

Last month, we were asked to help facilitate the drumming circle at Peregian Originals.  It was a short slot between sets, when the bands are packing down and setting up and we could see a few djembes in the crowd awaiting the moment. As soon as the band finished we called everyone into the centre of the grass area infront of the stage. It was early afternoon and the hot sun was beating down on us. As the drums got going more drums and drummers appeared out of the crowd until there was over 20 of us all sweating and smiling as we played a spontaneous groove together. The amazing Lee Hardisty joined us too, blowing funky middle eastern melodies on his saxophone. The band finished sound checking and as they starting playing we faded out and were left smiling with everyone dancing around us. Afterwards we had a refreshing swim and a serving of hot chips to finish the day off! So much fun!  Peregian Originals caught a great little [snap shot](https://www.facebook.com/PeregianOriginals/videos/10156688060335212/) of this moment and see below for our little video! What a glorious gathering by the ocean! East Coast Originals hosts [Peregian](https://www.facebook.com/PeregianOriginals) and [Cooroy](https://www.facebook.com/CooroyOriginals)  Originals monthly and an annual Originals Festival held in Noosa. The monthly events are free original live music events 100% crowd funded and so powered by the people that come and generously donate on the day as well as local businesses that give support! They showcase local original music is public parks where all of the community can gather to appreciate music together! A great way to support local music and your community!! https://youtu.be/OMgiPn326-E
